test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T12:28:32.1615527Z             "body": "This private local fork retains the original stdio MCP tools and adds bounded batch/durable-job execution. Acceptance remains incomplete and this PR stays draft.\n\nThe packaged runtime pins Playwright/core1.64.1 and deterministically adds explicit VP9 BT.601 matrix metadata at build time. Exact source/output hashes fail closed; bundled dependencies keep the prepared core private to this fork and production installs with scripts disabled verify provenance. No runtime interception or recorded-file rewriting is used as a product fix. External BrowserContext/remote-server hosts retain their encoder. See docs/DEPENDENCY_PATCHES.md for source hashes, licensing, upgrade review and the297-file payload tradeoff.\n\nLatest native85 at23b07fd: batch1131/3, original including legacy515/6, combined1646/9. Windows main never ran after installed controller journal init reached schema then timed out with worker exit unconfirmed. Linux22 install was canceled at the unchanged30m job limit, so its package/main tests never ran. Three297-file native installs completed; Docker verified the encoder hash and passed both endpoint tests. All three actual Codex clients completed1k, model0/owned0. Mac raw902/SDK995/sync973 and separate server997 still timed out; pipe1k passed. These samples do not clear old failures or change defaults.\n\nOriginal Linux172/0, Windows169/3, Mac170/2. Firefox VP9 color now passes all OSes; prior Mac gray cases passed this sample with source-paint witnesses, without proving old causes. Mac WebKit still decodes248/37/0. Windows WebKit WAV remains loading (probably, ready0/error0), VP9 reports probably but fails ready0/error4. Separate Firefox upload/legacy click and Mac Chrome capture failures remain. All24 new shadow/virtual cases passed. All17 completed-job logs plus the failed EOF first read are archived. Historical missing birth ledgers,136/142 process cohorts, unknown exits and remaining security/resource/profile/operator gaps remain unresolved.\n\nThis follow-up preserves failed package installations, adds finer fixed schema phases without changing SQL/deadlines/lease rules, and introduces bounded diagnostic-only color metadata copies. Copies must preserve encoded-stream hashes and never replace the original assertion; an isolated unpatched Firefox negative still exits1 with255/24/0. Local schema48/48 each Node22/24,14 applicable Node20 checks, fresh297-file scripts-disabled production verification, strict typecheck and generated-doc lint pass. Chromium/Firefox metadata controls2/2 each Node20/22/24; gated hydration/lazy append/offline-worker fixtures also pass all three Nodes. Full local original suite92/92 passed Node24 on the preceding runtime phase. WebKit engine unexecuted locally. No force/replay, timeout increase, default channel/transport change, historical ownership exclusion or debt clearance.\n\nNative86 atfd1939c is running:\n- [Local batch QA39773672301](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39773672301)\n- [Original CI39773672308](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39773672308)\n\nSource-specific evidence: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md, docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/evidence/native85-completed-archive.json, native85-summary.json and native86-local-final-proof.json. Pending results are not passes. No merge or publication is proposed.\n",
